\ runas.fam — `runas user group program args...`: the program run as that
\ user and group (runas must be root), waited for; its status runas's.
: t variable ;  : st variable ;
100 lit alloc t !
argn 4 lit u< if "usage: runas user group program [args...]" eputs 0A lit eputc 1 lit exit then
t @ 1 lit arg scpy 20 lit over c! 1 lit + 2 lit arg scpy 0 lit swap c!
"/proc/self/user" 1 lit open dup 0< if "runas: no /proc" eputs 0A lit eputc 1 lit exit then
dup t @ dup strlen write 0< if "runas: not allowed (only root may)" eputs 0A lit eputc 1 lit exit then close drop
3 lit arg dup 0 lit spawnv dup 0< if "runas: cannot run " eputs drop 3 lit arg eputs 0A lit eputc 1 lit exit then
st wait drop st @ exit
